id: pm-rust-zukw
title: Implement native claim and release with published CLI parity
description: "Match locked 2026.10.7 ownership transitions, refusal envelopes, durable history, and concurrent claim arbitration."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: conformance,ownership,rust
created_at: "2026-10-07T23:58:19.521Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T23:30:34.193Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T23:30:34.184Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T23:30:34.184Z"
author: codex-sol
parent: pm-rust-u4al
resolution: "Implemented and merged in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/68: native claim and release with published CLI parity and safe timestamp validation"
expected_result: The acceptance criteria recorded on pm-rust-zukw are met on main.
actual_result: "Merged in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/68 after its full CI, an isolated release gate and a CodeRabbit full review with every finding resolved; native claim and release with published CLI parity and safe timestamp validation"
comments[29]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T23:58:29.759Z",codex-sol,"Plan: implement native ownership transitions under the existing item lock and journal; compare item/history bytes and refusal envelopes with locked CLI 2026.10.7; verify a two-process race, behavioral revert, and both release-check environments."
  "2026-10-08T00:06:57.313Z",codex-sol,"Implementation now matches explicit-author claim/release storage and compact JSON receipts. Published probes established preset precedence, repeated claim no-op, empty release maintenance history, strict-policy release refusal, and terminal claim force override. Six simultaneous two-process claim races produced exactly one winner and valid published-verifier history. Final differential rerun and coverage gates remain to verify."
  "2026-10-08T00:09:31.434Z",codex-sol,"All four live ownership differential tests passed against locked CLI 2026.10.7: exact item/history bytes, complete success/refusal JSON and exit codes, active/stale lock behavior, and six independent two-process races. Behavioral revert replaced both SDK ownership methods with unavailable-command stubs while retaining compiled CLI/test surfaces: all four tests failed at runtime (exit 101), including zero race winners; source was restored afterward."
  "2026-10-08T00:17:54.672Z",codex-sol,"Initial release-check passed all 214 tests but correctly refused below-100 coverage. Added consumer and unit checks for invalid settings/authors, missing items, lock IO faults, foreign claim diagnostics, skipped claims, and interrupted release history append followed by journal recovery; no coverage exclusions or lowered thresholds."
  "2026-10-08T00:24:18.759Z",codex-sol,"Coverage refinement now includes terminal force/no-force, strict release refusal, takeover warnings, idempotent claims, in-progress release warnings, and retained closing summaries in the unit build as well as the live oracle build. Receipt dispatch returns its writer result directly, preserving failure propagation. Full thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-08T00:29:09.752Z",codex-sol,"Final-source behavioral revert repeated successfully: the unchanged four ownership differential tests compiled and all failed at runtime (exit 101); the existing create/update/comment/close differential passed as a positive control with ownership reverted. Restored source. Coverage refinement now exercises measured bounded lock wait in both consumer and unit builds."
  "2026-10-08T00:39:17.229Z",codex-sol,"Coverage diagnostics now reach 100 percent for lines, functions, regions, and branches after adding principal-only release and warn-policy ownership cases. Clean release gates and the isolated HOME gate remain to be run."
  "2026-10-08T00:48:45.840Z",codex-sol,"Implementation verified: both clean just release-check runs passed, including disposable HOME with global/system Git configuration disabled and no Git identity supplied. Each ran 219 tests in ordinary and instrumented passes; all 3367 lines, 290 functions, 5090 regions and 696 branches were covered at 100 percent. Locked CLI 2026.10.7 byte/envelope comparisons and all six independent two-process races passed in every gate. Behavioral revert compiled and failed all four ownership tests; the existing mutation differential passed as positive control. Feature remains open for orchestrator verification; ownership is being released."
  "2026-10-10T03:25:45.271Z",codex-sol,"Resume the existing #68 candidate at ea29da3aa8265b597595f0ed9a3c95be08da0dbb for a minimal Windows test-only correction. Run 37709763894 passes all tests but misses the diagnostic lock-read error and its outer propagation regions at mutation.rs 1828 and 1889. Extend existing unit and SDK fixtures with a real exclusive Windows file handle, exact OS error 32, unchanged item/history bytes, and successful retry after fixture cleanup. Preserve production code, coverage thresholds and the locked 2026.10.7 oracle. Primary codec repair remains independent in PR #72. Companion session pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10 is linked through https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion/tree/main/.agents/pm."
  "2026-10-10T03:31:53.785Z",codex-sol,"The existing Windows aggregate covered 3362/3363 lines and 5085/5087 regions: both missing regions are one diagnostic-read error propagation chain. Unit and SDK fixtures now use a real Windows exclusive read handle (share_mode(0)); they preserve item/history bytes and require a successful retry. Production code and the 2026.10.7 oracle remain unchanged. Windows all-target/all-feature cross-check and strict target Clippy passed. Required claim/release differential passed all four tests. The diagnostic regression passes; swallowing the native diagnostic-read error compiled but failed it at runtime (exit 101), then production source was restored byte-for-byte."
  "2026-10-10T03:54:38.923Z",codex-sol,"Final test-only correction verified: both ordinary and isolated-HOME just release-check passed, each with 219 ordinary and 219 instrumented tests. Coverage is exactly 3367/3367 lines, 5090/5090 regions, 290/290 functions and 696/696 branches (all 100 percent). Both gates include required locked 2026.10.7 oracle, formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit, Cargo audit and changelog check. PM-linked Windows GNU all-target/all-feature check and strict Clippy also passed. Native Windows execution remains the hosted CI receipt for the append commit. No production source, dependencies, oracle semantics, coverage thresholds or exclusions changed. Releasing ownership without closing; orchestrator verifies."
  "2026-10-10T03:59:41.965Z",codex-sol,"At append head 1a6d111685209f65023b7e08efd0c5e11af1592a, run 38022248758 passes the Windows exclusive-handle unit fixture but the new SDK fixture fails its exact-path assertion. Workspace::discover canonicalizes the storage root, whereas TempDir retains another Windows spelling; the assertion compared those spellings. Correct the fixture lock path to Workspace::pm_root().join(\"locks/sample-conv.lock\") and keep the exact OS error assertion. This is a test expectation correction, not a production error-propagation change. Previous ordinary and isolated-HOME Linux aggregates passed; latest native Windows evidence is still required."
  "2026-10-10T04:00:47.847Z",codex-sol,"Canonical SDK lock-path correction verified by the linked diagnostic consumer regression, Windows GNU all-target/all-feature check and strict target Clippy. Repeated the native-only error-swallowing proof with the corrected fixture: it compiled and failed at runtime (exit 101), then restored source byte-for-byte and the linked positive test passed. Production source, dependencies and locked 2026.10.7 oracle are unchanged from the original feature head. Local full ordinary and isolated-HOME receipts belong to append 1a6d111; the next append requires its own native CI aggregate receipt. Releasing ownership without closing."
  "2026-10-10T04:17:56.103Z",codex-sol,"Review finding 4216462799 after the preceding agent completed and released the clean PR #68 candidate. Reuse this ownership feature. Verify future timestamp recovery against a real held ItemLock for claim and release under force and permissive no-force policies, reproduce before correcting, preserve durable bytes and historical timestamps, then require full four-metric source coverage and strict release gates. This is the Rust native timestamp extension; no published CLI core defect is claimed. Companion context: pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10 via the existing published tracker-directory link."
  "2026-10-10T04:19:56.348Z",codex-sol,"Independent reproduction confirmed finding 4216462799 on the prior source: six real ItemLock SDK regressions compiled and failed at runtime (exit 101), covering claim/release with force, minimal preset without force, and custom force_required_for_stale_lock=false without force. Every case changed durable bytes and removed the active lock while the original guard remained alive. Published ClaimMutationOptions and ReleaseMutationOptions expose no timestamp; this finding belongs to the native extension. Locked time 0.3.55 provides OffsetDateTime::now_utc() and chronological PartialOrd. Add an ownership-only future-instant refusal before acquisition/recovery; preserve historical fixtures and existing concurrency/differential contracts."
  "2026-10-10T04:25:25.419Z",codex-sol,"Final fail-on-revert proof removed only the ownership future-instant guard: unchanged held-lock regressions compiled and failed 0/6 at runtime; the unchanged SDK/CLI consumer test compiled and failed 0/1 (both exit 101). With that guard absent, all four required published 2026.10.7 ownership differentials still passed, including their six process races and exact historical clocks, establishing a positive control. Restored production source byte-for-byte. Initial restored targeted PM-linked tests passed 6/6 and 1/1; full ordinary and isolated-environment release gates are next."
  "2026-10-10T04:38:20.908Z",codex-sol,"Stopped the first aggregate before completion: read-only inspection showed the published fixture runner clears process opt-outs and can access the host telemetry queue. This incomplete aggregate is not passing evidence. Add the published DO_NOT_TRACK=1 opt-out after environment clearing, preserving clocks, item/history comparisons and process races; use opt-outs for tracker and release commands as well. Existing host telemetry data is preserved without edits; earlier invocations were not explicitly isolated, so no no-telemetry receipt is claimed for those runs. Restart both full gates on the corrected fixture boundary."
  "2026-10-10T04:48:50.073Z",codex-sol,"Ordinary PM-linked just release-check passed with explicit telemetry opt-outs: formatting, strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, private-item rustdoc, required published 2026.10.7 tests, genuine source coverage, Cargo audit and changelog verification. Fresh coverage is 3372/3372 lines, 5098/5098 regions, 291/291 functions and 698/698 branches, all 100 percent with unchanged thresholds, inventory and exclusions. Saved source/test digests for final commit verification. The isolated-environment aggregate is running; the interrupted earlier aggregate remains excluded from passing evidence."
  "2026-10-10T05:01:37.062Z",codex-sol,"Both final-source PM-linked aggregates passed with telemetry opt-outs: ordinary and disposable-HOME/global-system-Git-disabled just release-check. Each ran 226 ordinary and 226 instrumented tests; 904 total passes across both aggregates. Both fresh reports cover 3372/3372 lines, 5098/5098 regions, 291/291 functions and 698/698 branches at 100 percent. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, required locked oracle, identity audit, Cargo audit and changelog verification all passed. Saved source/test digests match both receipts. Native platform execution remains a separate CI receipt at the pushed head; no core timestamp API defect or whole-CLI parity is claimed."
  "2026-10-10T05:02:03.551Z",codex-sol,"Final Windows GNU all-target/all-feature check and strict Clippy both passed through PM-linked tests. The ownership correction, six real held-lock regressions, SDK/CLI extension regression, published telemetry process opt-out, and actual boundary/revert documentation are ready for the existing PR #68. All executable source/test bytes match the passing ordinary and isolated aggregates. Release this claim while leaving the feature in progress for orchestrator verification; native CI will verify the committed head separately."
  "2026-10-11T05:06:23.675Z",codex-sol,"Updating PR 68 by merging current main, preserving reviewed ownership and future-timestamp validation. README.md is the only conflicted file; retain claim/release support and the published 2026.10.9 contract. Validate against TOON 0.6.1 and the expanded main oracle corpus at unchanged coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-11T05:07:56.447Z",codex-sol,"Ownership differential now creates the numeric-looking title 05, claims with message 0., and releases with message 05, exercising TOON 0.6.1 scalar and tabular quoting through exact item and history comparisons. Existing timestamp guard and all main conformance regressions are retained."
  "2026-10-11T05:15:24.692Z",codex-sol,"Current-main timestamp revert proof compiled successfully with only the pre-lock future-clock guard removed. All six unchanged held-lock regressions failed at runtime: 0 passed, 6 failed, exit 101. The SDK/CLI positive-control test is still running; original production bytes will be restored before acceptance gates."
  "2026-10-11T05:17:24.530Z",codex-sol,"The SDK/CLI future-ownership test also failed after guard removal: 0 passed, 1 failed, exit 101. Both negative commands compiled; unchanged tests ran against TOON 0.6.1. Original src/mutation.rs bytes were restored before the quoting proof and final validation."
  "2026-10-11T05:19:47.113Z",codex-sol,"The ownership quoting regression also fails under a native-only behavioral revert of the old decoder-based quote-safety rule: 0 passed, 1 failed, exit 101, after successful compilation. The locked 2026.10.9 oracle and expanded ownership test stay unchanged. Supported TOON 0.6.1 quoting code was restored byte-for-byte; full ownership differential and aggregates follow."
  "2026-10-11T05:38:16.369Z",codex-sol,"Full ownership differential passes against locked 2026.10.9 after the merge: 4 tests, 0 failures; all ownership policies, exact item/history bytes and envelopes, active/stale lock refusal and recovery, terminal/in-progress transitions, and all six two-process races. Main TOON quoting corpus and the future-clock guard remain intact. Starting full ordinary and disposable-HOME aggregates at unchanged source coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-11T05:53:00.276Z",codex-sol,"Matching CI runtime for final aggregates: Node 26.7.0, Rust 1.90.0, nightly-2026-08-06 branch instrumentation. Earlier unfinished Node 24 aggregates were stopped and are not passing receipts; completed ownership and native-only revert proofs remain independent receipts. No source assertions, coverage thresholds, or exclusions changed."
  "2026-10-11T07:15:13.514Z",codex-sol,"Current integration first full just release-check passed on Node 26.7.0: 227 ordinary and 227 instrumented tests, zero failures or ignored tests. Fresh executable-source coverage is 3353/3353 lines, 287/287 functions, 5062/5062 regions and 682/682 branches. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, Cargo audit and pinned changelog verification passed. The disposable-HOME aggregate is now running; its result is pending."
  "2026-10-11T07:47:23.829Z",codex-sol,"Final current-main receipts: ordinary-HOME and disposable-HOME just release-check both passed, each with 227 ordinary and 227 instrumented tests, zero failures or ignored tests. Both fresh reports cover 3353/3353 lines, 287/287 functions, 5062/5062 regions and 682/682 branches at the unchanged 100 percent thresholds. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, Cargo audit and pinned changelog verification passed. All 42 source, test, manifest and gate-input hashes match both receipts. Behavioral reverts compiled and failed the six held-lock guards, SDK/CLI timestamp regression and numeric ownership quoting sequence; restored ownership differentials passed 4/4 with six races. Evidence is updated in docs/OWNERSHIP_PARITY_2026_10_7.md. Releasing the claim while leaving this item in progress for review; no PR merge or item closure."
